{
  "_about": [
    "Where scripts/sync-drop-rates.ts finds a drop rate for each item on a Bosses or Raids collection log page (data/collection_log.json).",
    "Each page's rates are stored under `source` (default: the page name, which is what the plugin's log import matches on). `wiki` lists wiki pages whose drop tables count as that page, in priority order: the first one that drops an item wins. `Page#Fragment` picks one table on a page (e.g. the Corrupted chest). An object {page, via} means the rows on `page` are rolled per `via` item, so they're multiplied by the rate of `via`.",
    "`combine: \"independent\"` treats every listed table as a separate roll (the Colosseum's per-wave rewards). `variants` are extra sources for modes the game counts separately, so a live drop there is rated at that mode's rate; the page itself gets the first listed rate. `assumption` is copied into each row's metadata.",
    "When a kill-count message names the boss differently from its page's source (\"Dagannoth Rex\" vs \"Dagannoth Kings\"), add it to supabase/functions/_shared/kc-aliases.ts, which ingest-drop uses."
  ],
  "pages": {
